# Who may publish and subscribe to what. Anything not granted here is denied.
#
# Crew devices are addressed by device id (in Iridium SBD, the modem IMEI), not by crew or incident:
#   lookout/dev/{device}/up     device -> server: 16-byte positions, 8-byte acks
#   lookout/dev/{device}/down   server -> device: alerts of at most 270 bytes
# The server's device registry says which incident and crew each device reports for, and drops
# anything from a device it does not know. So a device login is confined twice: by this ACL to its
# own two topics, and by the registry to one incident and crew.

# The Lookout server: every device uplink, every drone survey and weather station; every downlink.
user lookout
topic read lookout/dev/+/up
topic write lookout/dev/+/down
topic read lookout/+/drone/front
topic read lookout/+/wx

# The field simulator plays every crew device, the drone and the weather station at once.
user field
topic write lookout/dev/+/up
topic read lookout/dev/+/down
topic write lookout/+/drone/front
topic write lookout/+/wx

# A real device logs in with its device id as username and can use only its own two topics.
pattern write lookout/dev/%u/up
pattern read lookout/dev/%u/down
